/**
@mainpage ESA code reference

ESA accepts manually forwarded snapshots and provides read-only engineering
advice. All code comments and generated documentation use English.

@section reference_map Code map

| Directory | Responsibility |
| --- | --- |
| `internal/esa` | Intake, snapshots, state transactions, shared investigations and review |
| `internal/codex` | Routing/engineering/assignment provider, source selection and citation validation |
| `internal/replaytools` | Capability-gated source/runtime tools, evidence IDs and cleanup |
| `internal/capabilities` | Operator-approved Profile and Skill contracts |
| `internal/replay` | Historical Jira reconstruction and frozen Git export |
| `internal/classifier` | Optional human-supervised label suggestions |
| `internal/retrieval` | Lexical Issue-directory search |
| `internal/codexreview` | Separate retrospective semantic-review contract |
| `system_replay` | Independent public-API tester and later Git repair checks |
| `scripts` | Operator commands, dataset handling and environment lifecycle |

Go files appear under Related Pages with AST-derived declarations, original Go
signatures, source locations and adjacent comments. Function bodies are omitted.
This is not a C++ translation or a Go type/call-graph analyzer. Python and Java
use Doxygen's native parsers. Ruby integration is described in @ref redmine_plugin;
Ruby and browser JavaScript symbols are not automatically indexed.

@section workflow_contracts Workflow contracts

Manual forwarding freezes input and cutoff. Routing reads a scoped local Issue
directory, reuses existing advice, joins work in progress, asks for information,
returns a support request, or requests engineering. At most three engineering
tasks run concurrently. Engineering reports evidence and a grouping request;
Routing makes the final Issue assignment. Review does not close Redmine issues.

Source/runtime tools require operator registration and granted capabilities.
Frozen inputs remain read-only; unchanged-source builds and diagnostic helpers
use scratch. Citation provenance, symptom reproduction and causal correctness
are separate checks. Cleanup owns only task-created resources.

The independent replay tester freezes initial public results before inspecting
future Git history. It does not substitute its own routing or engineering logic.
*/
